  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/wEV86Eh7pCJW3HXCzJ5UkjVE9Kfk1DYxoqgkgl5UaNg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nDue to \\(-\\mathrm{I}\\) and \\(-\\mathrm{R}\\) influence, \\(\\mathrm{NO}_2\\) in ortho-postion should have raised the acidity to the maximum extent. But it is due to intramolecular \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) - bonding, ortho-nitrophenol is less acidic than para - nitrophenol.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/kyFSdBc4cTv2AyixTimrpFvLCDbaQYnoJOxLnX9CHgE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
